{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774029050,"nonce":"4LRF11PkC3nYh9q6wnVY1fs3vbE=","title":"P6: Continuations lifecycle — dissolve into work units, Resume action","message":"Parent: f3dbb3e\nDepends on: 8a281b3 (P4 — work-unit model), 84cd5ae (P5 — issue hub UI)\n\nDissolve session-level continuations into the work-unit model. Add Resume action.\n\n## Continuation on work units\n- When a session ends (status → ended/dead) and has linked issues via session_issues:\n  - If the session has a continuation field: copy it to the work unit continuation column\n  - Set continuation_by = session_id, continuation_at = now\n  - Clear the session-level continuation (or mark as transferred)\n- For SDK sessions: Mandible detects session end via SDKBackend lifecycle. Write structured exit context (exit reason, last tool, cost, uncommitted changes) alongside free-text continuation.\n\n## Auto-ack\n- When a new session links to the same issue (via agent-commit or session registration): clear the continuation_by/continuation_at on the work unit (implicitly acked by pickup)\n- When work unit transitions to merged/abandoned: continuation is moot\n\n## Resume action\n- Issue detail \"Resume Work\" button: POST /api/issues/:repo/:id/spawn\n  - Creates SDK console session with: cwd = worktree path, provider_session_id from conversation, initial prompt injection with issue context + continuation text\n  - Updates work unit assigned_session_id\n  - Returns console_session_id, navigates to #/console?session=\u003cid\u003e\n- Inbox \"Resume\" button on continuation items: same flow\n\n## SDK auto-resume policy\n- New setting: auto_resume_policy = \"manual\" | \"auto_retry\" | \"auto_retry_with_limit\"\n- Default: \"manual\" (user must click Resume)\n- auto_retry: when SDK agent dies with non-terminal error, auto-spawn new agent with continuation context (max 3 retries)\n- Add to settings UI\n\n## Backward compatibility\n- External agents (third-class) still write session-level continuations via PATCH /api/sessions/:id\n- Inbox route: for orphan continuations (session has continuation but no linked issue), show as \"Unlinked handoff — [Attach to issue]\" with action to link\n\n## Inbox simplification\n- Continuations in inbox are now pointers to work units, not standalone items\n- \"Acknowledge\" button replaced with \"Resume Work\" and \"Dismiss\"\n- Dismiss just clears the notification; the continuation text stays on the work unit for reference","files":null}]}